# Fin cant (spin in flight): type a cant, see the canted fins in 3D and in the aft-view inset (Alt shows it: the env variable holds it for
# a script), drag the inset's cant handle, then fly it in Simulate and read the roll rate, the spin rows and the Roll plots.
#   BOWSHOCK_DRIVE_MODIFIERS=alt cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/cant.drive out/cant
# (Without the variable the viewport says `Hold Alt for the aft view · fin cant` on a selected fin set.)
viewport 1280x1000
# Turn the camera to the tail (drag the ViewCube round, click TAIL), select the fin group in the Station Lanes.
press (906, 118)
move (860, 118)
move (800, 118)
release (800, 118)
press (906, 118)
move (860, 118)
move (800, 118)
release (800, 118)
click (916, 124)
click (925, 824)
# Type 3 degrees into Cant: positive is clockwise seen from behind (the aft view says CW).
click (1175, 763)
type "3"
type enter
screenshot cant-1-aft-3deg.png
# Drag the cant handle of the inset round to the limit (15 degrees); the tag turns warn.
press (886, 218)
move (895, 222)
move (915, 232)
move (935, 250)
screenshot cant-2-drag.png
release (935, 250)
# Back to 3 degrees, then fly it: Simulate, Run selected, the Roll preset.
click (1175, 763)
type "3"
type enter
click "Simulate"
click "Run selected"
click "Roll"
screenshot cant-3-simulate-roll.png
